You can use the following function in C# to find duplicates in a collection:

```c#
public List<T> FindDuplicates<T>(IEnumerable<T> collection)
{
    List<T> duplicates = new List<T>();
    HashSet<T> set = new HashSet<T>();

    foreach (T item in collection)
    {
        if (!set.Add(item))
        {
            duplicates.Add(item);
        }
    }

    return duplicates;
}
```

You can call this function with your collection of items to find duplicates. It will return a list of items that are duplicates in the collection.

